ec05-49ac-8bcd-a5c757b30992"}],"related":[{"word":"uric acid"},{"word":"uridine"},{"word":"uridylate"},{"word":"uridylic acid"},{"word":"urine"}],"synonyms":[]},"uranus":{"id":"6d6a2757-7df5-4384-936d-7c021196ab17","word":"Uranus","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"god of the sky and heavens","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Urano"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"god of the sky and heavens","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Úrano"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"planet","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Urano"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"planet","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Úrano"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The giving the name of Uranus, however, to the planet of M. Herſchel, in which M. Bode ſtill perſiſts, is an act of ingratitude to the author of that noble diſcovery, and an affront to that auguſt and munificent patron of aſtronomy, the King of Great Britain ; whoſe name ought to be preferred to every other, if that of the author had not a ſtill more forcible claim on our acknowledgements. Beſides, the name of Uranus is an impropriety, even according to the mythological ſyſtem. Sanchoniathon and Diodorus, it is true, ſay, that Saturn was the ſon of Uranus; but this is now allowed to be purely allegorical.","ref":"1789 June, “LETTER from M. DE LA LANDE, on the NAME of the PLANET HERSCHEL, to the EDITORS of the JOURNAL des SCAVANS.”, in The European Magazine, page 437, column 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,29],[414,420],[555,561]],"id":"065580de-03b8-4ce2-9fb2-536ced64bee2"}],"topics":["astronomy","natural-sciences"],"wikidata":["Q324"],"senseid":["en:Q324"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Astronomy","en:Planets of the Solar System"],"links":[["astronomy","astronomy"],["planet","planet"],["solar system","solar system"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"Georgian planet"},{"word":"Georgium Sidus"},{"word":"H